# The kitty keyboard protocol's modifiers field. Under flag 1, Delete
# carries each of the eight modifiers in its own bit: Shift 1, Alt 2,
# Ctrl 4, Super 8, Hyper 16, Meta 32, Caps Lock 64 and NumLock 128, and
# the field is 1 more than the bits. A key that makes text drops the lock
# bits. Under flags 11, a modifier key's own event carries the state that
# the event leaves. When both Ctrl keys are held and one is let go, its
# release still has the Ctrl bit set. Caps Lock's press that turns the
# lock on carries the lock's bit, and the press that turns it off does
# not.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Modifiers, Event types, Disambiguate escape codes, Report all keys as escape codes, Functional key definitions; ADR-1005 D7
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
needs key-events
send "\e[>1u"
key Delete mods=shift
key Delete mods=alt
key Delete mods=ctrl
key Delete mods=logo
key Delete mods=hyper
key Delete mods=meta
key Delete mods=lock
key Delete mods=num
key Delete mods=shift+lock+ctrl+alt+logo+num+hyper+meta
key a mods=alt+num
send "\e[=11u"
cmd key;sym=ffe3;mods=4
cmd key;sym=ffe4;mods=4
cmd key;sym=ffe3;mods=4;event=release
cmd key;sym=ffe4;event=release
cmd key;sym=ffe5;mods=2
cmd key;sym=ffe5;mods=2;event=release
cmd key;sym=ffe5
cmd key;sym=ffe5;event=release
